    "format-version": "0.1",
    "license": "MIT",
    "name": "Cluster-guided comparative genomics",
    "readme": "This Galaxy workflow extends a previously published Galaxy-based WGS workflow for ESBL-producing Enterobacterales bloodstream isolates by adding cluster-guided comparative genomics analyses.\n\nInput genome assembly FASTA files are first grouped using dRep-based ANI clustering. QUAST assembly-quality metrics are used to support within-cluster reference-genome selection for Snippy/Snippy-core analysis. Prokka-generated GFF files are used for cluster-specific Roary pan-genome and core-gene analyses. Representative genome pairs per cluster are analyzed with MUMmer/NUCmer to evaluate local sequence-alignment structure. Roary core-gene alignments and Snippy-core SNP alignments are analyzed separately with IQ-TREE, and resulting trees are visualized in iTOL.\n\nDownstream analyses should be performed within ANI-defined multi-genome clusters. Singleton clusters are summarized but are not used for within-cluster MUMmer, Roary, Snippy-core, or IQ-TREE analyses.",
    "report": {
        "markdown": "\n# Workflow Execution Report\n\n## Workflow Inputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_inputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow Outputs\n```galaxy\ninvocation_outputs()\n```\n\n## Workflow\n```galaxy\nworkflow_display()\n```\n"
    },
